#question(title: [Average Velocity])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  You are traveling.  \
  Your position at time $t$ is $s(t)$.  \
  Your velocity at time $t$ is $v(t)$.  \
  The function $v$ is continuous on an
  interval $[a, b]$.

  Which of the following represent your
  average velocity on $[a, b]$?

  + $display((s(b) - s(a))/(b - a))$
  + $display(1/(b - a) integral_a^b v(t) d t)$
  + $v(c)$ for at least one $c$ between $a$
    and $b$
]
